GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC11): the steady overworld tells the window where the world and the
attached layer truly are, and keeps the world under the attached layer.

- GPU3D: ShownOrthoOrigin (where the world's origin truly is in the picture on screen: the scene's
  OrthoOrigin, the in-between's halfway) and ShownAttachTrue (where the attached layer's reference
  truly is), in the screen's columns and rows. The window slides the picture by a shift at the
  screen's resolution; at a scale that isn't whole (7.5) which game pixel gets one screen pixel
  more depends on where the picture lands within a screen pixel, so as the world moved (walking
  up, a quarter of a game pixel a frame) fine texture flickered (the user's play test, houses and
  the ground under the shadow). With these the window lands each on a whole screen pixel.
- GPU3D: the steady overworld's projection also puts the world's origin in the middle of a
  Z-buffer step: the camera's move along its view changed every depth by a fraction of a step,
  neighbours' depths rounded apart differently from frame to frame, and the lighting's normals
  (from those differences) flickered on walls, balconies and windows (the user's play test).

The software renderer's side of this patch (the world under the attached objects, their edges)
was replaced by patch 0026 (UC12).

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

